From 51df238e91533eddadb0c94d56aa2997b613a60a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pookee <13053375+pookee@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:52:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Up to four NSO GameCube controllers, players 1 to 4

iOS has no driver for the Switch 2's NSO GameCube controller. NSOGCKit
(apple/ios/NSOGC, from pookee/nso-gamecube-ios a6a82e8) connects it over
Bluetooth LE. The first controller is player one through the input mixer,
like a GameController pad, which it replaces while connected. Players 2 to 4
each get their own Dolphin pipe (GCPad2-4) and are plugged into their
GameCube port while connected, as a cable would (SerialInterface
ChangeDevice), except during an online match. The buttons map one to one,
with the triggers' analog travel and end clicks.

Controls menu: the controllers' status, Connect / Disconnect All / Forget,
and Hide Touch Controls with a Controller. Player one's input is published
on every report and the input tick is 120 Hz instead of 60 Hz.

Info.plist: Bluetooth usage text, and a meleepad:// launch link for
launchers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
